  "id": "mhande_karanga",
  "name": "Mhande (Karanga ceremonial dance-song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Ceremonial dance-song of the Karanga Shona of Masvingo province, performed in mukwerera rain-petitioning rites and in kurova guva, the ceremony that brings home the spirit of a deceased elder, where song and dance address the ancestors. It is sung in call and response to drumming, hosho rattles and hand-clapping, and has been documented in studies by the ethnomusicologist Jerry Rutsate. The generic membrane-drum card stands in for the ngoma drum.",
